{"count":12,"next_page":null,"page":1,"page_count":1,"per_page":25,"previous_page":null,"results":[{"id":900006470063,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900006470063.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900006470063-What-steps-can-I-take-to-avoid-hitting-the-rate-limit","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":2,"vote_sum":15,"vote_count":57,"section_id":900001810883,"created_at":"2021-04-07T17:25:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T12:14:23Z","name":"What steps can I take to avoid hitting the rate limit?","title":"What steps can I take to avoid hitting the rate limit?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-04-27T14:04:02Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eAll API keys come with a default limit of 20,000 requests per month. This is sufficient for most use cases but here are a few tips to making the most of your requests. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"\u003e\n\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eMake requests that return more results at once. All the endpoints that return multiple objects can be configured with `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003epage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e and `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eper_page\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e parameters for pagination. The maximum value of `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eper_page\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e is 80. You should request for as much data as necessary for your use case.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eImplement your own cache of responses from the Pexels API. URLs to our content returned from the API should not change over the short term, so serving them from your own cache would allow you to use Pexels content without having to use up your quota. 24 hours is a good amount of time to cache responses for.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"\u003e\n\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eIf you are making searches based on your users’ input, normalize the searches. A search for `\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\"\u003ec\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\"\u003eat\u003c/span\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e will return the same response as a search for `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003ecat\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e. Use this in conjunction with the caching described above.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eIf you still need of more requests, please see \"\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests-\" target=\"_self\"\u003eHow do I get unlimited requests?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\". \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"All API keys come with a default \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e of 20,000 requests per month. This is sufficient for most use cases but here are a","result_type":"article"},{"id":900005368726,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900005368726.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005368726-How-do-I-see-how-many-requests-I-have-remaining","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":3,"vote_sum":-1,"vote_count":51,"section_id":900001810883,"created_at":"2021-03-26T14:09:34Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T18:10:18Z","name":"How do I see how many requests I have remaining?","title":"How do I see how many requests I have remaining?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-04-27T14:05:43Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eEvery successful (`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e200 OK\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black50\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e) response contains 3 headers to help you manage your rate limit. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eX-Ratelimit-Limit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eYour total rate limit. All API keys have 20,000 by default until a rate increase is approved. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eX-Ratelimit-Remaining\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eHow many requests you have left before your rate limit is exceeded.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eX-Ratelimit-Reset\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eThe UNIX timestamp for when your rate limit will reset to the value in `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eX-Ratelimit-Limit\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black50\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eYou may want to keep track of the `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eX-Ratelimit-Reset\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black50\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e value if you think you are going to run out of requests because when the API responds with `\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-red110\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e429 Too Many Requests\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e, the header is presently no longer available.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"manage your \u003cem\u003erate limit\u003c/em\u003e. X-Ratelimit-\u003cem\u003eLimit\u003c/em\u003e Your total \u003cem\u003erate limit\u003c/em\u003e. All API keys have 20,000 by default until a \u003cem\u003erate\u003c/em\u003e increase","result_type":"article"},{"id":900005852323,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900005852323.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":3,"vote_sum":153,"vote_count":211,"section_id":900001840183,"created_at":"2021-03-12T04:03:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T13:58:51Z","name":"How do I get unlimited requests?","title":"How do I get unlimited requests?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-06-04T15:23:42Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWe're happy to remove the request limits on eligible applications but as this is our most asked question, we ask that you please review these requirements carefully.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur API keys come with the default rate limit of 200/hour and 20,000/month. Removing these limits is completely free but your platform needs to be eligible and meet our requirements. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eEligibility\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAPI users are bound to the same Terms and Conditions as Pexels users, which can be found in summary \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/license/\" target=\"_self\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. The added condition for API partners is that you \u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-underline\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003emay not\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/span\u003e copy our core functionality with the API. This includes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWallpaper apps\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUsing our API then promoting your site as a free stock platform\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnabling the selling of unaltered copies of a photo or video, (e.g. as a poster, print or on a physical product without modifying it first). \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEssentially, we look to ensure you're using our API to add a feature or build on an existing app or website that provides value beyond just our API. If you're looking to build an app or plug-in for a program (ie. WordPress, Figma, etc.) get in touch with us. We're happy to support (and even \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/pro/\" target=\"_self\"\u003efeature\u003c/a\u003e) community-built projects but we need to approve them first. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eRequirements\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePexels and our contributors must be credited within your platform. To verify this, we require either a mock-up, video or demo of how Pexels and the photographers are credited within your platform. You can review our guidelines \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/documentation/#guidelines\" target=\"_self\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and there are screenshots attached to this FAQ as examples. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"\u003eWhen you're ready, email \u003ca href=\"mailto:api@pexels.com\"\u003eapi@pexels.com\u003c/a\u003e with \u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-underline\"\u003eALL\u003c/span\u003e of the following:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"\u003eA short summary of what your platform is and how our library is being used\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"\u003eProof of attribution (either a video demo, screenshots or request a quick call with someone on our team)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"\u003eYour API key or the email address you registered with it\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"API keys come with the default \u003cem\u003erate limit\u003c/em\u003e of 200/hour and 20,000/month. Removing these \u003cem\u003elimits\u003c/em\u003e is completely free but your platform","result_type":"article"},{"id":900006376303,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900006376303.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900006376303-What-does-this-HTTP-response-code-mean","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":0,"vote_sum":-15,"vote_count":103,"section_id":900001810883,"created_at":"2021-03-30T22:44:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T05:48:07Z","name":"What does this HTTP response code mean?","title":"What does this HTTP response code mean?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2025-06-03T16:35:34Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\" style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable style=\"border-collapse: collapse; height: 105px; width: 106.429%; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: auto;\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"25px\"\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr style=\"height: 21px;\"\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"width: 232.273px; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e200 OK\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\" style=\"width: 489.727px; height: 21px;\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eYour API request succeeded.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr style=\"height: 65px;\"\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"width: 232.273px; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e401 Unauthorized\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\" style=\"width: 489.727px; height: 21px;\"\u003e\n\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eYou have not provided the proper Authorization header. See \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/documentation/#authorization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eauthorization\u003c/a\u003e \u003c/strong\u003esection in our documentation for\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e instructions about how to authorize your requests to the Pexels API.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr style=\"height: 21px;\"\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"width: 232.273px; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e403 Forbidden\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\" style=\"width: 489.727px; height: 21px;\"\u003eYou do not have access to the resource you are requesting.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr style=\"height: 21px;\"\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"width: 232.273px; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003e429 Too Many Requests\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\" style=\"width: 489.727px; height: 21px;\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eYou have exceeded your allocated rate limit. You are by default allowed to make at most 200 requests per hour and 20,000 requests/month. If you need a higher limit, learn how to get unlimited requests \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests-\" target=\"_self\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr style=\"height: 21px;\"\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"width: 232.273px; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e5xx Server Error\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\" style=\"width: 489.727px; height: 21px;\"\u003ePlease refer to our Help Article detailing common causes for this error and how to resolve them \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900006679223-What-if-I-encounter-an-error\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\"\u003e \u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"Too Many Requests You have exceeded your allocated \u003cem\u003erate limit\u003c/em\u003e. You are by default allowed to make at most 200 requests","result_type":"article"},{"id":14510573003673,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/14510573003673.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/14510573003673-How-to-upload-photos-and-videos-to-Pexels","author_id":379605381774,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":0,"vote_sum":77,"vote_count":147,"section_id":360007228174,"created_at":"2023-01-13T19:51:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T19:24:09Z","name":"How to upload photos and videos to Pexels","title":"How to upload photos and videos to Pexels","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2023-01-25T18:06:29Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":["upload","limits"],"body":"\u003cp\u003eBefore contributing to Pexels, it's important to review our \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/blog/resource/upload-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eUpload Guidelines\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUploading via Pexels on desktop and mobile\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e1. In order to contribute, you must first be signed in to your Pexels account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2. Once logged in, click on the \"Upload\" button in the top right corner of the site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3. On the \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/upload/\" target=\"_self\"\u003eUpload Page\u003c/a\u003e, drag and drop photo or video files into the area indicated or click the \"Browse\" button to browse the files you'd like to upload.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4. Adding a title, tags, or a location is all optional, but adding them will \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/blog/photography/photo-video-tagging-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehelp your content be discovered\u003c/a\u003e (you also have the option to participate in \u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042724994\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eChallenges\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e5. Click the \"Submit Content\" button\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUploading via Pexels iOS app\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e1. In order to contribute, you must first be signed in to your Pexels account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2. Once logged in, click on the \"+\" button at the bottom center of the app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3. Read the \"Confirmation of Media Rights\", check the box if you agree, and click the \"+ Upload Media\" button.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4. Select the photos or videos you'd like to upload and click \"Done\" in the top right corner\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e5. Adding tags, or a location is optional, but adding them will \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/blog/photography/photo-video-tagging-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehelp your content be discovered\u003c/a\u003e (you also have the option to participate in \u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042724994\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eChallenges\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e6. Click the \"Submit\" button\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"Before contributing to Pexels, it's important to review our Upload Guidelines. Uploading via Pexels on desktop and mobile","result_type":"article"},{"id":900005851863,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900005851863.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005851863-Do-I-have-to-pay-for-higher-limits","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":5,"vote_sum":25,"vote_count":73,"section_id":900001810883,"created_at":"2021-03-12T03:27:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:57:00Z","name":"Do I have to pay for higher limits?","title":"Do I have to pay for higher limits?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-03-23T18:48:08Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cdiv class=\"api-faq__question\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"api-faq__question__answer\"\u003eNope! Our API is free of charge. If you’re likely to hit the default request limits and you're able to provide and show acceptable attribution to Pexels and our contributors, limits can be lifted free of charge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"request \u003cem\u003elimits\u003c/em\u003e and you're able to provide and show acceptable attribution to Pexels and our contributors, \u003cem\u003elimits\u003c/em\u003e can be lifted","result_type":"article"},{"id":14886157597337,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/14886157597337.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/14886157597337-Is-there-a-limit-to-how-much-I-can-upload","author_id":379605381774,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":0,"vote_sum":48,"vote_count":70,"section_id":360007228174,"created_at":"2023-01-25T18:06:54Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T06:32:03Z","name":"Is there a limit to how much I can upload?","title":"Is there a limit to how much I can upload?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2024-02-16T03:40:46Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003eThere is no overall limit, you're able to upload as much as you want! We do have daily upload limits, though, with the ability to unlock unlimited uploads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat is the upload limit?\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eContributors are limited to 50 uploads per day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCan my limit be increased?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUnlimited daily uploads are exclusive to \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/hero\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ePexels Heroes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCan my limit be decreased?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe upload limit can be decreased if a contributor abuses their upload privileges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhen does the daily limit reset?\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eThe daily upload limit resets every day at 00:00 UTC.\u003cbr\u003eYou can check the \u003ca href=\"https://time.is/UTC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ecurrent time in UTC here\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"uploads. What is the upload \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e? Contributors are \u003cem\u003elimited\u003c/em\u003e to 50 uploads per day. Can my \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e be increased? Unlimited daily","result_type":"article"},{"id":47677890260761,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/47677890260761.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/47677890260761-Is-the-Pexels-API-free-to-use","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":true,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":0,"vote_sum":492,"vote_count":554,"section_id":900001840183,"created_at":"2025-06-04T19:36:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T01:58:08Z","name":"Is the Pexels API free to use?","title":"Is the Pexels API free to use?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2025-06-04T21:22:49Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553414,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp data-start=\"138\" data-end=\"184\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYes, the Pexels API is completely free to use.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-end=\"455\"\u003eEach API key includes default limits of 200 requests per hour and 20,000 requests per month. If you require higher usage, you can submit a request for unlimited requests. Please visit: \u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests\"\u003eHow do I get unlimited requests?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-start=\"583\" data-end=\"704\"\u003eTo explore available features, documentation, and other details, visit our \u003ca class=\"cursor-pointer\" href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"664\" data-end=\"703\"\u003eAPI page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"is completely free to use. Each API key includes default \u003cem\u003elimits\u003c/em\u003e of 200 requests per hour and 20,000 requests per month. If","result_type":"article"},{"id":900004904026,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900004904026.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900004904026-How-do-I-get-an-API-key","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":2,"vote_sum":387,"vote_count":765,"section_id":900001840183,"created_at":"2021-03-12T03:40:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T15:43:39Z","name":"How do I get an API key?","title":"How do I get an API key?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2025-06-05T19:56:06Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003eGreat question! It's easy, quick and free.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFirst review our documentation \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/documentation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThen create an account on Pexels \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/join-consumer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ehere\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRequest your API key \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/key\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou'll receive your API key immediately\u003c/strong\u003e. That API key is unique to you and will have default limitations on how many calls you can make. Please note that each user account is assigned one API key only.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 id=\"h_01JADPC18X23H1DFZ9MFMXWH5R\"\u003e \u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch3 id=\"h_01JADPC18X0FER3ADKG06TXJ8H\"\u003eGetting Unlimited Calls\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor most use cases, the default limit is more than enough. But if you're a high traffic platform, we're happy to lift those limits. Unlimited calls are still completely free, but we do need to verify your use case and review your attribution. You can learn more about getting unlimited calls \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"the default \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e is more than enough. But if you're a high traffic platform, we're happy to lift those \u003cem\u003elimits\u003c/em\u003e. Unlimited","result_type":"article"},{"id":360042725034,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/360042725034.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042725034-Can-I-submit-more-than-one-photo-or-video-to-a-challenge","author_id":370635304993,"comments_disabled":true,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":2,"vote_sum":60,"vote_count":98,"section_id":360007354933,"created_at":"2020-02-10T18:33:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T17:18:28Z","name":"Can I submit more than one photo or video to a challenge?","title":"Can I submit more than one photo or video to a challenge?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2020-02-19T14:37:49Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003eYes! There is never a limit to how many images or videos you can submit to any challenge you find on Pexels. After all, the more you submit, the higher your chance of winning!\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"Yes! There is never a \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e to how many images or videos you can submit to any challenge you find on Pexels. After all, the","result_type":"article"},{"id":900005538826,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900005538826.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005538826-Why-do-I-get-the-same-content-from-multiple-requests","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":1,"vote_sum":25,"vote_count":55,"section_id":900001810883,"created_at":"2021-04-07T18:00:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T12:09:48Z","name":"Why do I get the same content from multiple requests?","title":"Why do I get the same content from multiple requests?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-04-07T18:01:02Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003eThe Pexels API caches responses for 24 hours from the time they were first received. Additionally, while we do add new content constantly, the specific search you are making may not have new content since the last time it was requested.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-weight: 400;\"\u003ePlease note that making a request for a cached response will still count towards your request limit, but this may change in the future.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"for a cached response will still count towards your request \u003cem\u003elimit\u003c/em\u003e, but this may change in the future.","result_type":"article"},{"id":17635007931673,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/17635007931673.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/17635007931673-Do-I-need-certain-permissions-when-sharing-my-work","author_id":379605381774,"comments_disabled":true,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":0,"vote_sum":63,"vote_count":101,"section_id":360007228174,"created_at":"2023-04-17T18:23:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T07:37:50Z","name":"Do I need certain permissions when sharing my work?","title":"Do I need certain permissions when sharing my work?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2023-05-19T02:08:04Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"\u003cp\u003eWhen sharing your work on Pexels, you agree that you hold all of the proper rights and permissions to do so.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn particular, you agree that the work you are uploading is yours (you own it) \u003cstrong\u003eor \u003c/strong\u003eyou have the right to use it. When we say “the right to use it”, we mean that you have the proper permissions from any relevant third party who might hold rights in the work. This includes, but is not limited to, copyright, trademark or other intellectual property rights, contract rights, personality rights, privacy rights, data rights or other rights associated with any person or object featured in the work.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"wysiwyg-indent1\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExample\u003c/strong\u003e: An object in a photo or video (such as a visible logo on a car) might be protected by intellectual property rights, including copyright and trademark rights.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs the uploader, it is your responsibility to ensure that you hold all of the necessary rights and permissions for the work you are contributing to Pexels.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf any permissions are called into question, we respond to alleged violations of law and alleged copyright infringement notices in accordance with section 8 of our \u003ca href=\"https://www.pexels.com/terms-of-service/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eTerms of Service\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","user_segment_ids":[],"snippet":"might hold rights in the work. This includes, but is not \u003cem\u003elimited\u003c/em\u003e to, copyright, trademark or other intellectual property rights","result_type":"article"}]}